From b1e216da72fa1b473cd4b10aa053a26137baeb56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 09:23:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(editor): guard eight async effects whose cleanup only
 cancelled the timer, not the request
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every one of these cleared a debounce or interval on teardown and then let the
already-dispatched fetch resolve into a component that had moved on. Symptoms
users actually see:

- chat search, npm package search and the domain-availability lookup all paint
  results for a query the user has stopped typing, because a slow early request
  lands after a fast later one — and clear the spinner while the real one runs.
- the design-direction picker can fire onSkip() from a previous open and
  dismiss a modal the user is looking at.
- the sandbox live-sync effect re-runs on every edit; the superseded run still
  raises the destructive "Preview out of date" toast for a sync that has since
  succeeded, and its trailing timers flip the machine to "ready" underneath a
  sync that is still loading.
- site analytics let a 7d response (or a poll fired under the old range)
  overwrite the 90d data the user just switched to. The spinner gets its own
  token so a poll can never strand `loading` at true.
- the MCP context panel re-enables sources the user just disconnected when a
  refreshKey bump races the env lookup.

preview-annotations had a different bug in the same family: initial state is
seeded once from whichever project mounted first, so a project switch without a
remount kept the previous project's pins — and the persist effect then wrote
them onto the new project's cache and, once hydration settled, its chat-state.
Hydration now swaps in the incoming project's cache and the first persist pass
after a switch is skipped.

tsc --noEmit: 216 errors before, 216 after, identical set — no new type errors.
